# Story 33: Lanes (##lane / ##new lane) (40s)
# Hook: Lanes are the columns that organize your panes -- manage them directly.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-033-lanes.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Lanes are the columns that organize your panes -- manage them directly.

[00:03.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh and cycle into rysh mode with double-Escape.

[00:09.0 --> 00:16.0]
New lane adds a fresh column to the tab, ready to hold its own panes.

[00:16.0 --> 00:24.0]
Lane list shows every lane in the active tab with its identifier and contents.

[00:24.0 --> 00:31.0]
Lane info zooms into the lane holding your active pane -- its panes, groups, and flex weight.

[00:31.0 --> 00:40.0]
Lane name gives a lane a readable label, and lane delete removes one you no longer need. Lanes give your layout real structure.

